    {
      "id": "be543a84-ca00-40a0-9f6a-21bc1c2b6dbf",
      "name": "Sticky Note 549f6e88",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        190,
        190
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow A - Sensor monitoring & anomaly detection (Agent 1)\nTriggers: every minute, or immediately when the backend pushes new incident ids (authenticated webhook, header `X-Ghost-Token`).\n\n1. **Agent 1** runs in the backend (deterministic heartbeat + statistical rules; incremental: only new 15-min buckets are evaluated).\n2. **Claim** atomically reserves unprocessed incident versions (idempotent; no double processing; backend falls back to local processing if n8n is down).\n3. Each claimed incident goes through B -> C -> D.\n\n**Configure:** `apiBaseUrl` in *Config* (from WSL use the Windows host IP, e.g. `ip route | awk '/default/ {print $3}'`), and the two credentials. Keep inactive until both are set and a manual test passes.",
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1600,
        "height": 300
      }
    }
